MVP components (what they do)
1) Ingestion API

Endpoints like POST /ingest/org (body: { provider: "greenhouse", org: "acme" })

Validates and enqueues jobs to Job Queue.

Also has POST /ingest/discover to crawl a list of career URLs (for JSON-LD & sitemaps).

2) Fetcher Workers (adapters)

Small modules per source:

GreenhouseSource, LeverSource, AshbySource, SmartRecruitersSource

JSONLDSource (extract <script type="application/ld+json"> JobPosting)

SitemapSource (discover URLs; low frequency)

Each returns RawJob with external_id, company_domain, raw_description, apply_url, locations, posted_at.

3) Normalizer & Deduper

Maps fields into Job table (see schema below).

Idempotency key: sha1(company_domain + provider + external_id)
If a provider lacks external_id, hash (title + city + first_200_chars).

Versioning: if description / valid_through / salary changes, create a new job_version row; keep job.current_version_id.

4) Index Builder

Creates/updates tsvector fields (title, company, location_names, skills, description_excerpt) and refreshes materialized views for facets.

Emits “new matches” for Saved Searches (alerts).

5) Public API

GET /jobs (filters: keyword, location, remote, salary, seniority, company, posted_since)

POST /saved-searches → alert channel (email/push, daily/instant).

POST /applications (user adds an applied job to tracker).

Later: GET /recommendations (skills-based).

6) Web App (Next.js) + minimal mobile

Search + filters, job details, “Save”, “Alert me”.

Tracker: add application, stage, notes, due dates.

Prep: 3 curated tracks (SWE/PM/DS) with checklists and mock-interview booking (Calendly link v0).

Optional extension v1: “Recognize ATS form → Prefill”.